/-
P3 (line mmuAD, gen 32): **`jat_scheduleFR` over `JAtZB`** — XTopJointSchedR's `jat_scheduleFR` (FL4's
`sched.schedule` against the spec's `schedule` after the fired timers) with `JAtZ` → `JAtZB`, and the scheduler
chain it needs that was missing over `JAtZB` (generated by `scratch/mmu32_jatzb_gen.py`): `JAtZB.usrWJ`, `bufAtJ`,
`schedPreW`, `deadP_sch_step`, `sch_frame` (its `JExt` conjunct dropped: `JAtZB` has none), `sch_buf`, `sch_apart`,
`sch_jpl` (bare `nodeW` → `Sched.nodeW`: inside `JAtZB.*` it would resolve to `JAtZB.nodeW`), `sch_kern`, `sch_csc`, `sch_utc`, `sch_tail`, then **`JAtZB.jat_scheduleFR`**: premises exactly the
original's with `JAtZ` → `JAtZB` (`hVt` over `JAtZB` states, `hSig : SignalJHypB` [J] of JAtZBFire) and without
`[VxE Z]`, post without `RJ` (it packs a `JAtZ`, i.e. `JExt`, which a VM-epoch state does not have).

`jat_scheduleSR` over `JAtZB` is not stated: it needs `signalJHypB_of` (ScSignalJ's `signalJHyp_of` over `JAtZB`,
the waking-signal chain), see JAtZBFire's docstring for why the remaining `SignalRestJHyp` case is a [J].
No new premise beyond JAtZBFire's `SignalJHypB`; no existing statement changed.
-/
